<span class="cat-badge">Guide &middot; Local Areas</span>
<h1>French Quarter by Motorbike: Motorbike Route Connections in Hanoi</h1>
<p>The French Quarter&rsquo;s greatest riding asset is not its own streets, lovely as they are, but its connections, the formal grid south and southeast of Hoan Kiem Lake reaching out to the Old Quarter at its shoulder, the lake districts to the north, the wide city to the south and the river bridges east toward the rental counter at Long Bien. A rider based here is connected to the whole central map by short, legible legs, and the skill the quarter asks is the planner&rsquo;s one, knowing which line serves which trip and at which hour. This page reads those connections honestly, without fabricated journey times, because duration is the day&rsquo;s own fact and the honest guide teaches the shape, not the stopwatch.</p>
<p>The rental counter is at Motorbike Rental - Nguyen Tu, 112 Nguyen Van Cu in Long Bien, across the Red River, and the connection to it is the plan&rsquo;s spine. Start at the <a href="/motorbike-rental-hanoi-old-quarter/">Old Quarter motorbike rental</a> hub, see the machines and verified prices at the <a href="/hanoi-motorbike-rental/">Hanoi motorbike rental</a> guide, browse the wider <a href="/motorbike-guides/">motorbike guides</a>, read the <a href="/motorbike-rental-hanoi-old-quarter/hoan-kiem-route-connections/">Hoan Kiem route connections</a> page for the district-level network, and see the <a href="/motorbike-rental-hanoi-old-quarter/ba-dinh-route-connections/">Ba Dinh route connections</a> page for the landmark district to the north.</p>
<nav class="toc">
<ol>
<li><a href="#sec-1">The quarter&rsquo;s position on the map</a></li>
